# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. Contact form email — Gmail SMTP setup
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Copy this file to `.env.local`
# 2. Sign in to https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords and
#    generate an app password for "Mail" (requires 2FA enabled).
# 3. Paste the 16-character password below.
# 4. Restart `npm run dev`.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

SMTP_USER=vbphotograph2015@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your-16-char-app-password

# Optional — defaults shown
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# CONTACT_TO=vbphotograph2015@gmail.com


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   2. Cloudflare R2 — image CDN
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Full setup walkthrough: docs/CLOUDFLARE_SETUP.md
#
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_CDN_BASE_URL is required for the site to serve
# from R2 — the others are only used by `npm run upload`.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Prefix Next.js prepends to every /assets/... URL.
# Leave blank in dev to serve photos from the local public/assets folder.
# In production (Render/Vercel/etc.), set this to your R2 public URL:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_CDN_BASE_URL=https://pub-abcdef123456.r2.dev
# or your custom Cloudflare-fronted domain:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_CDN_BASE_URL=https://img.vbphotographe.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_CDN_BASE_URL=

# Only needed for `npm run upload` — the sync script that pushes photos
# from your machine into the bucket.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=vb-photographe
